Mechanism confirmed: attribute_effect's is_select effect calls `select_option(select, prev.value)` with undefined value → not mounting → selectedIndex = -1. Fix: only call select_option if 'value' in prev (or next), or pass mounting. Actually the effect runs once at mount (prev undefined → prev.value undefined). Guard: skip when value === undefined. Compare with `if (inited && is_select && 'value' in next)` — the immediate block path. The post-effect should match: only call when value was specified. Fix: 

```js
effect(() => {
    if ('value' in prev) select_option(select, prev.value);
    init_select(select);
});
```

Also init_select's observer callback uses select.__value — fine.

Record hypotheses, then patch.

